From cdc64718bbf47c397ac50cac55c6391c36ca0a3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahari Zahariev <harryzz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 07:46:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] WasmGC: add WEBASSEMBLY_GC_WASI target (JS-free WasmGC + real
 WASI floor)

Adds a new TeaVMTargetType.WEBASSEMBLY_GC_WASI that emits a WasmGC module
free of the JS-embedding runtime (no teavmJso, no wasm:js-string, no
teavmConsole/teavmDate/teavmMemory host imports), suitable for non-JS
component-model hosts (e.g. wasmtime via the preview1->preview2 adapter).

Target plumbing:
- Platforms.WEBASSEMBLY_GC_WASI + PlatformDetector.isWebAssemblyGCWasi()
  @PlatformMarker, so classlib can branch at compile time.
- TeaVMWasmGCHost.isWasi(); WasmGCTarget.setWasi(): adds WEBASSEMBLY_GC_WASI
  to platform tags, drops the env memory import (memory becomes internal),
  exports "memory" for WASI, makes heap globals internal consts, and routes
  intrinsics with the wasi flag.
- TeaVMTargetType.WEBASSEMBLY_GC_WASI + TeaVMTool wiring (reuses the WasmGC
  target with setWasi(true), emits classes.wasm).
- JSOPlugin and TThrowable skip JS interop / JS stack capture under WASI.

Real WASI floor (only these two host imports, both wasi_snapshot_preview1):
- stdout/stderr: WasmGCSupport.putChar* route to fd_write (gated on
  isWebAssemblyGCWasi); browser keeps teavmConsole.
- wall clock: System.currentTimeMillis -> WasmGCSupport.currentTimeMillis via
  clock_time_get (SystemIntrinsic emits the call under wasi; linked through
  WasmGCDependencies.contributeWasi so dependency analysis includes it);
  browser keeps teavmDate.
- heap growth: Heap.grow stays the memory.grow intrinsic; notifyHeapResized
  is skipped under WASI (self-managed, no host callback).

Browser WEBASSEMBLY_GC output is unchanged (still teavmJso/js-string/teavmDate,
zero wasi imports). Verified end to end: Java -> WasmGC-WASI core -> preview1
adapter -> WASI 0.2 component (imports wasi:cli/io/clocks, exports custom
verbs) running under wasmtime.
